@file 195:
@file 196: ## Well taps
@@file 197: delete_inst -inst *WELLTAP* ;
**WARN: (IMPSYC-295):	Found no instance name matching wildcard "*WELLTAP*"
@file 197: # In case any well taps has been placed prior, delete these
@file 198: # Set well tap cell to be used
@@file 199: set_db add_well_taps_cell HS65_LH_FILLERNPWPFP4
@file 200:
@file 201: # Create well taps
@file 202: # Explanation : We need to add well taps, to bias the bulk of the transistors to the correct potential
@file 203: #               According to the documentation, the maximum distance a cell can have to a well tap is 30um.
@file 204: #               This means that if we space the well taps with 60um, all cells will be within the 30um range of a tap.
@@file 205: add_well_taps -cell_interval 60
**WARN: (IMPSP-362):	Site 'CORE' has one std.Cell height, so ignoring its X-symmetry.
Type 'man IMPSP-362' for more detail.
Estimated cell power/ground rail width = 0.325 um
For 7270 new insts, Inserted 7270 well-taps <HS65_LH_FILLERNPWPFP4> cells (prefix WELLTAP).
@file 206:
@file 207: #Add pad fillers
@file 208: set leftPads [get_db [get_db insts -if {.lib_cells == *IO65*}] -if {.orient == r270}]
@@file 209: deselect_obj -all
@@file 210: select_obj $leftPads
@@file 211: add_io_fillers -cells [get_db [get_db base_cells -if {.name == *IOFILLER?_*LIN}] .name] -side left -filler_orient R270
